0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $2$ |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299803 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4fa12227-09f8-5d99-a2be-207b65a88fe1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299803 #edb/ref 1074 "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3}-1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1069 "q-319943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5aecc675-116f-5b56-855b-8a2ff5a85c00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299811 #edb/ref 1074 "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-20-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-26\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}78 \\\\ -52 \\\\ -182\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1069 "q-320021" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$ABC=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34cd5f5a-f82e-5ae5-899e-5e1bd32cf8b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299814 #edb/ref 1074 "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $(AB)$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)\\,C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24 & 48 & -60\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324039 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324039 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324039 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0768e386-ed42-523a-8b81-d32778b33888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324697 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324697 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324697 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5765f40b-6dcf-5301-9949-f4819aec1ba2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325158 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325158 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325158 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8bca11ec-165a-537d-b134-38df44b671e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325358 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begi